Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 03:26:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(room): fully qualify the claude-room image
 (bounded-systems/claude-box#245)

`claudeRoom.image` was the bare `claude-box`, so `prx pod up --pod per-repo`
rendered `image: "claude-box"` into the kube-play manifest and podman expanded
it against Docker Hub on any host without a local image:

    unable to copy from source docker://claude-box:latest

The published image is `ghcr.io/bounded-systems/claude-box/claude-room:<release>`
(claude-box's publish-ghcr workflow: nix attr `claude-image` -> GHCR `claude-room`).
Pin that ref as an exported `CLAUDE_ROOM_IMAGE` constant, matching the
sibling rooms (BEADSD_ROOM_IMAGE, KEEPERD_ROOM_IMAGE, CONCIERGED_ROOM_IMAGE),
at the latest claude-box release tag (0.7.0). A digest pin + BOX_PINS entry
can follow once the (currently private) GHCR package's digest is readable.

Tests: assert the claude-room image is registry-qualified and not `:latest`,
and that no perRepoPod room image can fall back to a docker.io short name;
the kube-render test now checks the constant rather than the bare name.

Refs: https://github.com/bounded-systems/claude-box/issues/245

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
